Data   : the web HelpPage has NO API data source — it renders a short, intentionally-stable curated link palette
         unconditionally (web/src/features/system/pages/HelpPage.tsx HELP_LINKS). HelpPageViewModel therefore exposes
         a static StateFlow<UiState<HelpContent>> seeded directly in the Content phase carrying HELP_LINKS; no
         loading/empty/error transitions are reachable because the content is local + always available, so none are
         fabricated (no stub states). The AI surface the web page layers alongside (AIRAGHelp) is a separate,
         conditional component / parity unit outside this page's allowed files — intentionally not mounted here
         (its off-mode contract is "renders nothing").
Strings: all 12 page keys already present in res/values/strings.xml (translation_help_title, translation_help_intro,
         and the five translation_help_baseline_links_<id>_{title,description} pairs, generated by the shared i18n
         catalog) — no string-catalog edit needed; every literal resolves via stringResource(R.string.translation_*).
Nav    : the page is UNROUTED in web/src/App.tsx (no /help route), so it is intentionally absent from the
         generator-locked Destinations registry (DestinationsTest pins Destinations.all.size == 137; count UNCHANGED).
         A7 wires it as a standalone deep-linkable composable in TeslaSyncNavHost under route "help" with deep links
         teslasync://app/help + https://app.teslasync.io/help (built from RouteTable.APP_SCHEME/APP_HOST), host via
         PageHosts.register(help){ HelpRoute() }. Each curated card opens its existing canonical destination
         (/docs/status-api, /onboarding, /system-status, /search, /chatbot) through the app's own teslasync://app/{path}
         scheme (AndroidManifest scheme=teslasync host=app + TeslaSyncNavHost) via LocalUriHandler, since no
         NavController is exposed to page hosts.

